Mobilization Products  IFC promotes development by mobilizing financing for the private sector in its developing member countries. Mobilization at IFC is governed by  IFC's  Core  Mobilization  Procedure  (the  Procedure). The Procedure interprets how the harmonized MDB/DFI mobilization  definitions  of  mobilization  apply  to  IFC's private-sector development activities. IFC estimates Core Mobilization at the time of commitment based on the project financing plan. Mobilization activities are included in Core Mobilization if they meet five criteria:
Sourced from a third party that is neither IFC nor the client itself;
Include financing or credit-risk transfer;
Arranged on commercial terms;
Due to the active and direct involvement of IFC; and
Benefit an IFC client.
